@startuml sim_dotbot_mrta_ws_target_class_diagram

title sim_dotbot_mrta.py — MRTA mode class design (mrta_mode/ over mapf-simulation's core + pibt)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ClassBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassHeaderFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C060

package "mrta_mode (WS-driven position, REST as fallback only)" #E8F5E9 {

    class GridStateManager <<REST client>> {
        + base_url : str
        + cell_mm : int | None
        + map_cells_x, map_cells_y : int
        --
        + fetch_dotbots() : list[dict]        <GET /controller/dotbots>
        + fetch_map_size() : (int, int)       <GET /controller/map_size>
        + set_map_size(width_mm, height_mm) : void
        + mm_to_cell(x_mm, y_mm) : Coordinates2D
        + cell_to_mm(pos) : (float, float)
        + resolve_conflicts(positions) : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
    }
    note bottom of GridStateManager
      Not the step-loop's position source. Used once at
      startup (map size + initial bot list) and by
      ControllerStatusListener as the degraded-mode
      fallback when the WS link is down -- GET
      /controller/dotbots, off the hot path.
      Coordinates2D is frozen, hashable, .x/.y.
    end note

    class ControllerStatusListener <<WS client>> {
        + ws_url : str                         <ws://.../controller/ws/status>
        - _stop : Event
        --
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        - _listen_forever() : void
        - _handle_raw(raw) : void
        - _dispatch(notification) : void
    }
    note bottom of ControllerStatusListener
      Single WS connection. _dispatch() reads both payload
      shapes carried by cmd=2 (UPDATE):
        - data.lh2_waypoints -> click_events queue
          (consumed by ManualClickTranslator)
        - data.lh2_position  -> LivePositionStore.update()
      Reconnects with backoff on drop.
    end note

    class LivePositionStore {
        - _positions : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        - _updated : dict[str, Event]
        --
        + update(address, position_mm) : void
        + snapshot() : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        + wait_until_all_arrived(targets, timeout) : set[str]
    }
    note bottom of LivePositionStore
      Arrival is event-driven: wait_until_all_arrived()
      blocks on per-bot Events set by update(). If no WS
      update arrives before `timeout`, falls back to one
      GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots() call -- same safety
      net as ManualClickTranslator.reconcile().
    end note

    class ManualClickTranslator {
        - _commanded : dict[str, Coordinates2D]
        --
        + seed_commanded(dotbots_raw) : void
        + record_commanded(address, cell) : void
        + translate(waypoints_mm, current) : list[Coordinates2D]
        + is_self_commanded(event) : bool
        + reconcile() : list[ClickEvent]         <-- REST fallback,
                                                       GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots()
    }
    note bottom of ManualClickTranslator
      mm<->cell translation, dedup, and self-echo detection
      (telling a manual click apart from the echo of a PUT
      this script itself just sent, arriving back on the
      same WS channel). reconcile() is the REST safety net
      for clicks made while the WS link was down: compares
      GET /controller/dotbots' `waypoints` against what the
      script last sent.
    end note

    class WaypointCommandClient <<write-path only>> {
        + base_url : str
        + threshold : int
        --
        + send(address, waypoints_mm) : void          <PUT /controller/dotbots/{address}/0/waypoints>
        + send_all_parallel(moved_mm) : void           <N parallel PUTs, same route>
        + send_stop(address) : void                     <PUT ... {waypoints: []}>
    }
    note bottom of WaypointCommandClient
      Issues commands only. Arrival-waiting lives in
      LivePositionStore, which holds the live data.
      The WS status channel is broadcast-only from the
      controller; commanding a bot always needs this PUT.
    end note

    class MRTASession <<activatable mode>> {
        + engine : WorldEngine
        + agents : list[Agent]
        - _orchestrator : LifelongGoalOrchestrator
        - _active_target : dict[int, Coordinates2D | None]
        - _pending_chain : dict[int, deque[Coordinates2D]]
        --
        + connect() : void
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        + halt_all() : void
        + handle_click(event: ClickEvent) : void
        + tick() : void
        + run() : void
        - _advance_chain(agent_id) : void
    }
    note bottom of MRTASession
      **tick()** is the plain step -> send -> wait, no
      pipelining: a manual click can land mid-travel and
      must be reflected in the very next advance_time_step(),
      so pre-computing ahead would miss it. Arrival wait is
      LivePositionStore.wait_until_all_arrived().

      **handle_click()** translates the waypoint chain to
      cells via ManualClickTranslator. Empty chain (Stop-nav,
      or nothing to do) -> cancel: set_target(agent_id,
      agent.position) so assign_missions() clears the slot
      next tick (position == target), and drop any queued
      chain. Non-empty chain -> set_target(agent_id,
      cells[0]) (overwrites any in-flight target
      unconditionally -- the orchestrator's own contract, so
      a re-click needs no separate cancel) and store
      cells[1:] in _pending_chain[agent_id].

      **Multi-hop waypoint chains are MRTASession's job.**
      LifelongGoalOrchestrator holds one mutable target slot
      per agent, no queue. After each advance_time_step(),
      for every agent at its target with a non-empty
      _pending_chain, _advance_chain() pops the next cell and
      calls set_target() again. _active_target mirrors the
      orchestrator's private _target dict (MRTASession is the
      only caller of set_target()) and drives the idle
      check: sleep when no agent has a target and no events
      are queued.
    end note

    class MRTACli <<CLI driver>> {
        --
        + main() : void
    }
}

package "mapf-simulation (external repo, pip-installed -- core + pibt)" #EAF4FF {
    class WorldEngine
    class Grid2D
    class Agent
    class Objective
    class AssignmentManifest
    class StepOutcome
    class PathPlanner <<interface>>
    class MissionOrchestrator <<interface>>
    class PIBTPlanner
    class LifelongGoalOrchestrator
    PathPlanner <|.. PIBTPlanner
    MissionOrchestrator <|.. LifelongGoalOrchestrator
    WorldEngine *-- PathPlanner
    WorldEngine o-- MissionOrchestrator
    WorldEngine *-- Agent
}
note bottom of PathPlanner
  Imported from the pip-installed `mapf-simulation` package
  -- top-level `import core` / `import pibt`, no sys.path
  insert. core provides Agent / Grid2D / WorldEngine /
  Coordinates2D; pibt provides PIBTPlanner and
  LifelongGoalOrchestrator. WorldEngine composes a
  PathPlanner (PIBTPlanner) and a MissionOrchestrator
  (LifelongGoalOrchestrator).
end note
note bottom of LifelongGoalOrchestrator
  One mutable target slot per agent
  (`_target: dict[int, Coordinates2D | None]`), written only
  through set_target(agent_id, position). No shared pool,
  no arbitration between agents: the caller that owns the
  goal source decides per agent.

  - **Eligibility** is moot: set_target() takes an explicit
    agent_id, and a click already means "this one bot".
  - **Idle / parked** is built in: assign_missions() clears
    an agent's slot to None the instant position == target
    and omits it from goals; it stays parked until
    set_target() is called again. Matches MRTA's "every bot
    starts parked" invariant.
  - Requires PIBTPlanner's GoalReachedPolicy.TRANSIENT (its
    default): an agent demoted to -inf priority on arrival
    is undemoted the instant it is re-targeted.

  Left to the caller (per pibt/AGENT.md), and owned by
  MRTASession: multi-hop waypoint chains (one slot, no
  queue) and preventing two agents being set to the same
  target.
end note

MRTASession *-- GridStateManager
MRTASession *-- ControllerStatusListener
MRTASession *-- LivePositionStore
MRTASession *-- ManualClickTranslator
MRTASession *-- WaypointCommandClient
MRTASession *-- WorldEngine
MRTASession *-- LifelongGoalOrchestrator
MRTASession o-- Agent

ControllerStatusListener ..> ManualClickTranslator : click events\n(data.lh2_waypoints)
ControllerStatusListener ..> LivePositionStore : position events\n(data.lh2_position)

ManualClickTranslator ..> GridStateManager : uses (mm_to_cell,\nREST fallback)
LivePositionStore ..> GridStateManager : REST fallback only\n(WS outage)
WaypointCommandClient ..> GridStateManager : uses (cell_to_mm)

MRTACli ..> MRTASession : builds & runs (CLI driver)

@enduml
